A||N||5||Vlad||How to disconnect Cold Start Enjector....?||||1||
Z||000000||Vlad||05-14-2001||02:14 AM||||<BR>Actually, how to disconnect it I pretty much understand, but I can't get which one.<BR>There are two ejectors (or switches) in my V6. First is right under the distributor and another one is behind thermostat housing.<P>Now, my intention is to disable cold start system and see how it affects fuel consumption which is currently 15 MPG.<P>So which one of those two things should I disconnect?<P>Thanks||||reg||1
Z||000001||mrfiero||05-14-2001||02:36 AM||||It's behind the distributor.  Push in on the silver clip while pulling on the plug and it'll unplug.  <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||Vlad||05-14-2001||02:46 AM||||<BR>Can you please explane what is the purpose of the thing behind the thermostat housing provided that the CS enjector (valve that actually enjects fuel) is under the distributor?||||reg||1
Z||000003||Ken Wittlief||05-14-2001||08:30 AM||||Simply unplugging your CSI will not prove its not the problem - It could be leaking, and if you unplug it then it will continue to leak.<P>   OK well acutally, if you unplug it and the car starts easily when its cold that might be a sign that its leaking?!<p>[This message has been edited by Ken Wittlief (edited 05-14-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000004||87GTZ34||05-14-2001||10:50 AM||||Vlad - the 'thing' by the thermostat is the actual CS switch.  It also has a clip like the fuel injectors do.  The one by the dist is the actual injector.  It has a small fuel line that runs into the fuel rail.  The CS injector is only activated during cranking from the solenoid circuit.  The CS switch just allows current to pass if the eng is cold.  If you disconnect it you may only see that it is a little harder to start.  If it is leaking, it will continue to do so and you wont see any difference in perf.  To chek it, take the injector out, reconnect the fuel line only, put a rag over the injector'to soak up fuel' and make sure you catch whatever runs out in a container and not on your eng or floor.  DO NOT START IT but turn the key to the on position (with injector harness disconnected) and if any fuel runs out, that injector is leaking. Replace if necessary and reassemble and that one will be eliminated.<p>[This message has been edited by 87GTZ34 (edited 05-14-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000005||WisconsinGT||05-14-2001||11:35 PM||||Anyone know where I can get a new CSI? Thanks!||||reg||1
